# Research first (before any new page)

1. One primary query; name intent (do / know / compare / navigate); match page type.
2. Skim top 5 results: format, questions answered, gaps — plan one differentiator (worked example, table, reverse mode).
3. Check `docs/KEYWORD-MAP.md` for cannibalization; extend an existing URL instead of duplicating intent.
4. List 3–6 secondary / PAA questions → H2s and FAQ.

Full checklist: keep this rule aligned with the shared per-page checklist (titles, schema, mobile, sources).

# Structure

- One H1 matching the query in plain words.
- **Answer first:** opening 40–60 words answer the query with a number or clear verdict.
- **Tools:** dropzone / first input above the mobile fold (390×844). ≤60 words between H1 and the tool. Byline and long privacy copy **after** the tool. Cookie banner ≤56px and must not cover the dropzone.
- **Guides:** `.answer-box` immediately after H1 (before byline). Key takeaways next. Byline after takeaways.
- H2/H3 in order; worked example with real numbers; at least one table/diagram you made; unique body (no copy-pasted Operations notes across guides).
- Visible published / last-updated dates matching schema + sitemap lastmod.

# Metadata & schema

- Title 30–60 chars (CI also allows 25–65), unique, primary query near start, brand at end.
- Meta description 70–155 (CI 70–160), unique; og/twitter description identical.
- Canonical absolute, self-referencing, https, trailing slash; `absoluteUrl()` / `PUBLIC_SITE_URL` only — never hardcode hosts or `example.com`.
- `og:image` absolute URL must not end with `/`.
- Tool pages: WebApplication + FAQPage (3–6 visible Qs) + BreadcrumbList; Hammad byline; ≥1 topical guide link; Person `@id` `https://github.com/hammadiqbal6#person`.
- Guides: Article + FAQPage + BreadcrumbList; ≥800 words; author/dateModified match visible text.
- No fake ratings. JSON-LD must parse and match visible content.

# Claims & privacy

- Do not claim “works offline” / service worker unless a real SW is shipped and tested.
- Separate “file bytes never upload for conversion” from “page analytics may load.”
- No AdSense placeholder / stub text in HTML when ads are disabled.
- Cite primary sources for numbers; no invented credentials or benchmarks.

# Ship

- Add `docs/KEYWORD-MAP.md` row; page in sitemap; `npm test && npm run build && npm run audit` (includes `audit:pages`).
- Governing playbooks: `docs/SEO-PLAYBOOK.md`, `docs/SEO-GUARDRAILS.md`, `docs/CUSTOM-DOMAIN.md`.
